{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018DeYFa3y5QJFqAnTtYzBM1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that regenerates GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verifying behavioral parity via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Human writes PRDs/use cases; mage-claude-orchestrator generates Go code in `cmd/` and `pkg/`; `pkg/testutils` runs differential tests comparing Go binaries against GNU references.\n\n**Current state:** 15 releases specified (rel00.0 through rel05.4 plus rel99.2). All show `codestatus: not started` in the analysis. The generation branch has two prior commits for the checksum quartet (tasks 360, 361).\n\n**Current release:** rel05.4 — checksum quartet (md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum). All four use cases are at `spec_complete` / `codestatus: not started`.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 05.4 contains four use cases that are structurally identical — each reads files/stdin, computes a cryptographic hash, and prints `hash  filename`. They differ only in the hash algorithm (MD5, SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-512). Go's `crypto/*` packages provide all four algorithms. These utilities share flag semantics (`--check`, `--binary`, `--text`, `--quiet`, `--status`, `--strict`, `--warn`) and output format. A single task covering all four is appropriate given their trivial divergence and the 250-line budget.\n\nThe two existing commits (tasks 360, 361) on this branch suggest prior stitch attempts. The analysis still shows `not started`, so I propose the implementation task.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Task 362: Implement checksum quartet cmd/md5sum, cmd/sha1sum, cmd/sha256sum, cmd/sha512sum (rel05.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd017-checksums.yaml (all requirements for md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc001-md5sum.yaml (use case for md5sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum.yaml (use case for sha1sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum.yaml (use case for sha256sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum.yaml (use case for sha512sum)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.4.yaml (test suite for the checksum quartet)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared protocols section -- differential testing pattern, SIGPIPE handling)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests signature)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (reference for existing cmd/ package structure and differential test pattern)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (reference for differential test file structure)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: md5sum implementation using crypto/md5\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gmd5sum\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha1sum implementation using crypto/sha1\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gsha1sum\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha256sum implementation using crypto/sha256\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/sha256sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gsha256sum\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha512sum implementation using crypto/sha512\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gsha512sum\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement cmd/md5sum, cmd/sha1sum, cmd/sha256sum, cmd/sha512sum as standalone\n          Go binaries. Each reads files listed on the command line (or stdin if no files\n          are given) and prints the hex-encoded hash followed by two spaces and the\n          filename (or dash for stdin). Use crypto/md5, crypto/sha1, crypto/sha256, and\n          crypto/sha512 respectively from Go's standard library.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Support --check (-c) mode: read lines in the format \"hash  filename\", recompute\n          the hash for each file, and report OK or FAILED. Support --quiet (suppress OK\n          lines), --status (no output, exit code only), --strict (warn on improperly\n          formatted lines), and --warn (-w, warn on improperly formatted lines to stderr).\n          Exit 0 if all checks pass, 1 if any fail.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Support --binary (-b) and --text (-t) mode flags. On Unix these do not change\n          behavior (files are read identically) but affect the output format: binary mode\n          prints \" *filename\" (space-asterisk), text mode prints \"  filename\" (two spaces).\n          Default to text mode on Unix, matching GNU behavior.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for each utility. Each test file defines a\n          []testutils.DiffTest slice and calls testutils.RunDiffTests comparing the Go\n          binary against the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gmd5sum, gsha1sum, gsha256sum,\n          gsha512sum). Use exec.LookPath to find the reference binary and t.Skip if not\n          found. Test cases must cover: single file, multiple files, stdin, --check mode\n          with valid and invalid checksums, --binary flag, and missing file error.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          All four utilities share the same flag parsing and I/O logic. Each main.go\n          follows an identical structure, differing only in the hash.New constructor\n          import (crypto/md5, crypto/sha1, crypto/sha256, crypto/sha512). Do NOT create\n          a shared internal package -- keep each cmd/ package self-contained with its own\n          main.go, duplicating the ~50 lines of shared logic. This matches the project\n          pattern where each cmd/ package is independent.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of each main(), matching the\n          shared protocol from ARCHITECTURE.yaml. Import pkg/sys for this call only.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          In --check mode, match GNU output exactly: \"filename: OK\" or \"filename: FAILED\"\n          on stdout. On completion, if any files failed, print a summary line\n          \"prog: WARNING: N computed checksums did NOT match\" to stderr. If --strict or\n          --warn is set, print \"prog: filename: improperly formatted checksum line\" to\n          stderr for malformed lines.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          For differential tests, use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") to compile the Go\n          binary. Reference binaries are gmd5sum, gsha1sum, gsha256sum, gsha512sum\n          (Homebrew GNU coreutils). Follow the graceful-skip pattern:\n          exec.LookPath(\"g<utility>\") with t.Skip if not found.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: Each of cmd/md5sum, cmd/sha1sum, cmd/sha256sum, cmd/sha512sum compiles with \"go build ./cmd/...\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/md5sum/... ./cmd/sha1sum/... ./cmd/sha256sum/... ./cmd/sha512sum/...\" reports no issues\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Each utility produces correct hex hash output for a single file, multiple files, and stdin\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Each utility --check mode correctly validates checksums and reports OK/FAILED matching GNU format\n      - id: AC5\n        text: Differential tests pass against Homebrew reference binaries (or skip gracefully if not installed)\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/md5sum/... ./cmd/sha1sum/... ./cmd/sha256sum/... ./cmd/sha512sum/...\" passes\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27549,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27549},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b387ff8-6cc8-43d1-8937-09f55296dc95","uuid":"870d6769-d3f4-4904-80cf-e3273aa8078c"}
